mission "The Shipwright's Secret"
    name "The Shipwright's Secret"
    description "Take Tomas's secret harbour plan to Havana and help him expose Vane's hidden shipyard."
    source "Port Azure"
    destination "Havana"
    lead "Marta taps a note pinned behind the tavern bar. “A shipwright in Port Azure has been buying unusual quantities of copper sheathing and pitch. Don Esteban is honest, and he has asked me to send anyone who might understand why. You may find him near the long quay when your course takes you east.”"
    reward 540
    speaker offer "Tomas, the Shipwright"
    speaker visit "Don Rafael, Captain of the Watch"
    speaker complete "Don Rafael, Captain of the Watch"
    to offer
        has "The Gallows Tide: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `A broad man with burned hands is repairing a fishing boat on the quay. He introduces himself as Tomas, the shipwright Marta mentioned. He keeps his voice low and his eyes on the water.`
            `"Vane forced me to build a warship for him in a hidden yard inside Havana's outer harbour. I drew the plans before I escaped. The governor's officers have sealed the old eastern channel, but I know a way through the reefs."`
            choice
                `"I'll take your plans to Don Rafael."`
                    goto accept_job
                `"Why should I trust you?"`
                    goto details
                `"Keep your plans. I'm not going to Havana."`
                    goto decline_job
            label details
                `Tomas shows you a scar across his palm. "I built the guns that killed my own crew. Vane made me do it. I will not build another ship for him. Rafael can compare these plans with the harbour works. He will see I am telling the truth."`
                choice
                    `"I'll get the plans to Rafael."`
                        goto accept_job
                    `"Your trouble is not mine."`
                        goto decline_job
            label accept_job
                `Tomas rolls the plans into a copper tube and hands it over. "Follow the coast, not the main channel. The reefs are marked in red. If anyone can get through, it is a captain who has already faced Vane's guns."`
                accept
            label decline_job
                `Tomas returns to his work. "Then I will find another way to stop him."`
                close
    on accept
        log "Tomas has entrusted you with plans to Vane's hidden shipyard. Deliver them to Don Rafael in Havana."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Don Rafael studies the plans, then calls for a harbour pilot. The pilot traces the red line with a trembling finger. It leads behind the old fort and into a sheltered cove.`
            `"This is no ordinary dockyard," Rafael says. "Vane is building a warship there. The governor has been hiding it from the Crown and from the people of Havana."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Rafael rolls the plans and locks them in his dispatch case. "We cannot storm the yard yet. The harbour guns are watched, and Vane has spies in every tavern. We need proof that the governor's own fleet has been compromised."`
            `He takes a tarnished brass compass from his coat. "This belonged to the captain of a Spanish patrol ship that vanished near Port Royal. The compass was recovered from a wreck, and it points to a hidden anchorage used by Vane's couriers. Take it to Nell. She can identify the ships that come and go."`
        log "Delivered Tomas's shipyard plans to Don Rafael. A brass compass may reveal Vane's secret anchorage."
